WEBVTT

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:03.210
If you lose in the Friendship Cup,

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:08.190
you're sent to an underground 
forced-labor facility, never to return.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:12.260
While Mr. Tokumatsu was telling 
me that secret information,

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.890
Shinji and Layra were being chosen 
for the next match.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:20.130
Why don't you want to fight?

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.600
Because he's afraid, obviously!

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:28.360
C-Crow's... friend...

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.710
He gave me... candy.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.950
Back then...

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:41.150
You don't want to fight someone 
who showed you kindness.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:42.940
Tsukikage...

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:43.580
Sir.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:45.920
You will fight in Layra's place.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:46.940
Yes, sir.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:52.100
The one entering the arena is... Tsukikage?

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.300
Why did the pairing change?

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:56.640
No one told me about this.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:05.950
Well, that is... As you can see...

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:09.690
For some reason, there's apparently 
been a pairing change.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.900
This is how Tops always do things.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:16.090
They do whatever they want, 
only thinking of themselves.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:20.060
They treat us Commons like insects!

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.250
How vulgar.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.260
This is why I can't stand Commons.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:27.260
But we Commons share the blame.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:29.690
No matter what they do to us, we just roll over.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:32.650
We threw away our pride long ago!

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.710
We've been tamed.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:35.950
Shut up!

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:38.650
Get off the stage!

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:44.150
How rude! Stop picking a fight with the spectators!

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:47.620
I escaped from prison.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:53.210
But the authorities captured me and sent me here.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.830
They want to make an example of me!

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.410
I won't roll over for them.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.360
I won't be shamed!

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.940
I'm going to overturn this ridiculous society!

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.910
Oh, what are you talking about?

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:10.880
Why did you have to say that, 
after the arena was finally united?

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:14.840
A duelist should fight fairly, as befits a duelist!

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:18.660
Shinji, what are you planning?

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:39.870
Sorry I'm late.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:46.550
D-Wheels.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:50.760
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:52.480
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.920
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.090
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:35.450
Battlewasp — Summoning Swarm

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:38.940
City is united as one! We're all friends!

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:42.090
Let's brush off this anxious mood 
and build some hype!

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:46.990
I'm sorry for requesting the change.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:48.300
Forgive me.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.640
It's no great problem.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.990
Tsukikage, who's gone in his stead,

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:56.410
is combat-trained, proficient in ninja-style duels.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:05:00.200
I vouch for his ability. You may expect a good show.

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:05.260
Brother... Why?

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:09.030
Why did you put Tsukikage in instead of me?

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:11.190
Now, let's go!

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:13.260
Action Field, on.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.660
Field Spell Crossover Acceleration!

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:25.000
Riding duel...

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.210
Acceleration!

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:28.440
Duel!

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.710
Even if it is to protect Layra, 
to send Tsukikage out...

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:38.080
How can he do this, knowing what could happen?

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:41.180
Brother put him over me.

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:48.150
Neither Tsukikage nor that Commons 
boy will last for long.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:52.540
They're both heading for the 
corner at full acceleration.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:54.970
Tsukikage is the first to pass the corner!

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.540
It is my turn!

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:00.790
I summon Twilight Ninja Shingetsu from my hand!

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:08.070
And I activate my Continuous Spell 
Illusion Ninjitsu Art of Hazy Shuriken!

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:12.080
When I add a card to my hand,

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:16.450
I can send that card to the graveyard, 
to deal 300 damage to you.

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:17.910
Hazy Shuriken!

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.960
He isn't waiting around, is he?

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:26.330
A ninja... How lovely.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:28.170
What an interesting trick.

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:29.700
Bravo!

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:34.250
And once more... Hazy Shuriken!

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:39.370
Once more.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:40.780
Take this!

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.450
Three hits in the first turn!

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:47.920
It isn't over yet.

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:51.930
I won't let this end with a ninja show!

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:04.500
Shinji cuts off Tsukikage, as he 
goes for the Action Card!

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:08.840
I set one card and end my turn.

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:14.670
Shinji's at a disadvantage, right off the bat.

00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:16.510
What will he do on his turn?

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:19.600
I'm used to starting at a disadvantage.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:21.250
I'm not bothered in the least.

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:22.700
My turn!

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:26.140
I summon Battlewasp — Arbalest the Rapidfire!

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:30.730
Battle!

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:34.170
More Hazy Shuriken?

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:38.370
It won't keep you from losing 
your monster in this battle.

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:41.110
Arbalest, attack Shingetsu!

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:45.850
Continuous Trap Illusion Ninjitsu Art of Hazy Toad!

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:49.240
During your turn, by sending one card 
from my hand to the graveyard,

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:53.450
I can increase one Ninja's attack points 
by 1000 until the end of the battle.

00:07:56.590 --> 00:07:59.820
Oh, dear! Shinji took 700 damage!

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:04.260
But when Arbalest is destroyed,

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:08.470
I can Special Summon another 
Arbalest from my hand.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:16.330
I see. So even if one is defeated, 
a new one rises to take its place.

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:18.980
This is the way real Commons fight.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.180
Real Commons?

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:22.430
Real?

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:26.950
Probably because we have 
to stick together to survive.

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:31.000
When battle is over, Hazy Toad's effect ends,

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.630
and Shingetsu's attack points return to normal.

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:35.830
I now end my turn.

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:39.950
The Fuma Clan's bonds are no 
less strong than your own.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:41.800
My turn! Draw!

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:45.040
If Tsukikage wins...

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:48.670
Spell card Ninjitsu Art of Hazy Duplication.

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:52.520
I Special Summon one Ninja, Level 4 
or below, from my hand.

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:56.670
If Tsukikage wins, I...

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:00.870
Don't leave me! Don't leave me, Brother!

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:05.160
I Special Summon Twilight Ninja Shingetsu!

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:11.760
Summoning another weak monster 
won't help you at all.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:13.470
Are you so sure?

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:16.590
I tribute Twilight Ninja Shingetsu,

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:19.860
to Tribute Summon Twilight Ninja Nichirin, the Chunin!

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:27.040
If one's power is insufficient, stronger allies 
appear, with the force of the whirlwind.

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:29.110
This is the nature of the Fuma Clan's bonds!

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:30.320
Battle!

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:32.780
Nichirin attacks Arbalest!

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:37.960
With attacks from all sides,

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:41.080
Tsukikage continues to deal damage every turn.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:45.430
Shinji's in trouble! If he loses any more life points...

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:47.900
I have allies, too!

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:49.670
When Arbalest is destroyed,

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:52.900
I can Special Summon another 
Arbalest from my hand!

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.810
I end my turn.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:04.120
Even if they're knocked to the ground, 
my Battlewasps just build a nest there.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:06.550
Like the noble Commons children!

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:09.840
Did you know this?

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:13.590
They say when wasps build nests close 
to the ground, a hurricane is coming.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:17.360
I do not make light of the bonds 
or nobility of the Commons.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:19.100
Glad to hear it.

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:21.790
But that's easy to say.

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:25.500
I'm going to make you understand 
what a real Commons is!

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:27.210
My turn!

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:30.670
I'm sick of being on the losing end...

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:33.180
I'll sting you until you swell up like a balloon!

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:38.170
I summon Tuner Monster Battlewasp — 
Sting the Poison!

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:45.620
Level 2 Sting the Poison tunes 
Level 4 Arbalest the Rapidfire!

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:52.200
Flap your wings to stir up a shockwave...

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:55.100
Let your sting open up the road of truth!

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:56.970
Synchro Summon!

00:10:57.310 --> 00:11:00.440
Come, Battlewasp — Halberd the Charge!

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:03.680
Shinji has completed a Synchro Summon!

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:08.710
Battle! I attack Shingetsu with Halberd the Charge!

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:10.190
I won't allow it!

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:16.120
Illusion Ninjitsu Art of Hazy Toad!

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:21.340
I send one card from my hand to the graveyard, 
to increase one Ninja's attack points by 1000.

00:11:22.190 --> 00:11:24.030
But Halberd's effect...

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:27.470
When this card does battle with a 
monster with higher attack points,

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:29.700
it halves that opponent's attack points!

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:30.480
What?

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:36.970
Shinji finally takes a hit!

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:46.520
You spent a card on a power-up, 
only to take big damage.

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:49.290
I set one card and end my turn!

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:55.760
You rich Tops might end up the same way.

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:58.350
The more indulgently you live your life,

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:01.230
the bigger the shock when you take a hit!

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:04.350
That boy is a troublesome one.

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:05.440
Indeed.

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:08.240
Stop abusing the spectators!

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:11.040
The Friendship Cup isn't about that stuff!

00:12:11.390 --> 00:12:14.910
Denouncing spectators who have 
nothing to do with this...

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:17.280
You call yourself a duelist?

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:20.570
You're taking the Tops' side?

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:24.840
I guess that makes sense. Ninjas sneak around, 
doing dirty work for their lords.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.020
What do you mean by that?

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:30.030
You're as worthless as the Public Order Bureau,

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:31.730
which serves at the whim of the Tops.

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:35.700
Damn you! Are you calling my 
Fuma Clan worthless?!

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:37.300
Lose.

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:42.010
My brother gave his life to 
see his mission through!

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:43.210
Lose.

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:48.180
In the name of my proud brethren, 
I cannot ignore those words!

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:49.670
Lose!

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:57.390
My turn!

00:12:57.760 --> 00:13:01.950
When Twilight Ninja Nichirin, the Chunin 
is on the field, it is treated as a Ninja.

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:05.360
By tributing it, I perform a Tribute Summon.

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:09.980
I shall teach you the true power 
of a venerable Fuma ninja!

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:12.570
Twilight Ninja Getsuga, the Shogun!

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:18.730
Level 8 Getsuga can be Tribute Summoned 
with only one Ninja tribute.

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:21.780
So the boss is here, eh?

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:26.720
By switching Twilight Ninja Getsuga, 
the Shogun to defense position,

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:30.730
I can Special Summon two Ninjas in my graveyard!

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:35.420
Return to your shogun's side, 
Twilight Ninja Shingetsu!

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:38.160
When Shingetsu is on the field,

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:42.400
you cannot attack any Ninja but it.

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:48.110
And having two Shingetsus on the field 
means that Shinji can't attack Getsuga!

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:49.310
What?

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:51.920
And even if he gets past that,

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:57.010
he still has a big monster, with 3000 
defense points, to beat!

00:13:57.010 --> 00:13:59.720
This is Tsukikage's powerful... no,

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:01.960
far-too-powerful, iron-wall defense.

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:04.510
What will Shinji do? What should Shinji do?

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:07.230
And Tsukikage gets another Action Card!

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:10.540
Continuous Spell Ninjitsu Art of Hazy Shuriken!

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:15.530
I send a card I just added to my hand to the 
graveyard, to deal 300 damage to you!

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:19.800
How far will you go before you're satisfied?

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:24.920
Damn. Nothing's ever gone my way.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.940
Ever since I was a kid!

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:32.160
Listen up... This is no longer your house.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:34.220
Quit hanging around and get lost!

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:39.660
That's right. The orphanage that took me 
in was confiscated by debt collectors.

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:42.460
I even lost my home.

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:49.170
Be that as it may, it is no reason for 
you to disparage the Fuma Clan!

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:53.770
Hazy Shuriken!

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:56.470
Just like that...

00:14:56.470 --> 00:14:57.880
Hazy Shuriken!

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:05.820
They threw away the cards they 
stole from me, like garbage.

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:12.200
You dueled, when this was all you had?

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:14.940
Come back when you have some proper cards.

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:17.400
But I guess that isn't possible for a Commons...

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:21.530
Tops came to challenge Commons

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:24.770
to battles, where they had the 
advantage, to steal their cards!

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:27.240
They steal everything from us!

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:31.440
Is that how Shinji's felt all this time?

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:34.570
Shinji! I'm with you!

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:37.740
Those Tops destroy everything they touch!

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.530
Shinji, you'd better not lose!

00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:42.150
Go! Crush them!

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:47.360
This duel is a microcosm of society.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:51.000
They call it free competition, but the 
winners just keep winning.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:55.290
This is how City really works!

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:57.900
Now, stand up! Rise up!

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:02.340
Your eyes aren't dead anymore.

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:04.810
Fight! Raise your fists!

00:16:10.510 --> 00:16:14.250
This is the only place where our City is one!

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:16.690
City is one...

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:18.420
City is one.

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:43.650
City is one! City is one! City is one!

00:16:53.390 --> 00:16:55.360
Hazy Shuriken!

00:16:56.460 --> 00:16:57.610
I won't let you!

00:16:57.610 --> 00:16:59.810
Action Spell Stand Up!

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:04.640
I negate effect damage dealt by you 
this turn, and then end my turn!

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:08.860
We're quite stubborn, you see.

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:09.680
We?

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:12.830
That's right. On my next turn,
it won't just be me.

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:15.110
All of the Commons will stand against you!

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:18.010
Let's go! My turn!

00:17:20.860 --> 00:17:22.050
Draw!

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:24.790
Draw!

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:28.680
At last, the hurricane is here.

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:30.950
And it's gonna be a big one.

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:39.610
I activate my spell card Summoning Swarm!

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:42.840
I can Special Summon as many 
Battlewasps, Level 4 or below,

00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:46.110
as you have monsters on your side of the field.

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:49.080
You have three monsters in all.

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:51.800
I Special Summon my two Arbalests

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:55.380
and Tuner Monster Sting the 
Poison from my graveyard!

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:05.260
Go further! Do more!

00:18:05.260 --> 00:18:08.700
Rage like a wasp, whose nest has been kicked!

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:19.940
Shinji! Shinji! Shinji! Shinji!

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:39.460
This is getting dangerous. Call for 
security reinforcements.

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:45.230
So he says, but that could spark a riot.

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:47.370
We cannot have that.

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:50.580
What is this? A duel like this...

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:54.580
I activate Sting the Poison's effect!

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:59.950
I can tribute one Battlewasp to negate 
the effect of one of your monsters.

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:03.000
I tribute one Arbalest the Rapidfire

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:05.520
to negate the effect of one Shingetsu.

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:13.260
Battle! The other Arbalest attacks a Shingetsu!

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:21.140
And Halberd attacks the second Shingetsu!

00:19:24.800 --> 00:19:28.780
But Getsuga, the Shogun has 3000 defense points!

00:19:29.050 --> 00:19:30.570
Don't underestimate me.

00:19:30.570 --> 00:19:33.190
I activate my trap card Urgent Tuning!

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:38.390
This card allows me to perform a 
Synchro Summon during battle.

00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:39.220
What?

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:45.470
Level 2 Sting the Poison tunes 
Level 6 Halberd the Charge

00:19:45.470 --> 00:19:48.700
and Level 4 Arbalest the Rapidfire!

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:55.600
Let the power of solidarity's bonds

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:58.150
spear through the walls of 
overwhelming, disdainful evil!

00:19:58.580 --> 00:20:00.040
Synchro Summon!

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:06.520
Appear, Level 12 Battlewasp — 
Ballista the Armageddon!

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:16.630
Ballista the Armageddon's effect activates!

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:20.520
I banish all Battlewasps in my graveyard.

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:23.660
And for each monster banished, I reduce the

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:26.970
attack and defense points of 
one of your monsters by 500.

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.040
I banish five monsters.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:34.390
Thus, Twilight Ninja Getsuga, the Shogun's 
defense is reduced by 2500!

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:36.950
Now, Tsukikage will...

00:20:36.950 --> 00:20:41.920
Battle! Ballista the Armageddon attacks 
Twilight Ninja Getsuga, the Shogun!

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:47.600
When Ballista the Armageddon attacks 
a defense-position monster,

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:52.860
it deals piercing damage, equal to the difference 
between attack and defense points!

00:20:58.740 --> 00:21:01.710
Unbelievable!

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:13.150
In the second match of the day, 
the winner is Shinji Weber!

00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:15.690
Don't cheer! Rise!

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:17.440
What do you think you're doing?

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:19.120
Is making noise all you can do?

00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:23.440
Act! Fight! Fight already!

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:26.620
If Shinji is taking action, I should, too.

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:30.120
But I would just worry the kids more...

00:21:30.570 --> 00:21:38.280
Shinji! Shinji! Shinji!

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:41.210
What a magnificent duel.

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:43.480
It was almost like a riot...

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:46.430
He just got them riled up.

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:51.960
If a real riot had occurred, I would 
round up the lot of them.

00:21:54.720 --> 00:21:56.860
The second of them has lost.

00:21:56.860 --> 00:21:57.830
Yes.

00:21:58.320 --> 00:22:02.170
That means Tsukikage will also be sent 
to the underground labor facility.

00:22:04.310 --> 00:22:06.410
This was within the bounds of my plan.

00:23:48.560 --> 00:23:50.410
Enjoy Chojiro's opponent

00:23:50.410 --> 00:23:54.810
will be our first female duelist, Yuzu Hiiragi!

00:23:54.810 --> 00:23:58.220
To send this pretty little girl to the labor facility...

00:23:58.220 --> 00:23:59.840
Forgive me!

00:23:59.840 --> 00:24:03.550
Right now, Yuya must be berating himself.

00:24:03.550 --> 00:24:09.730
But I'll give everything I have, 
to show that he isn't alone.

00:24:09.730 --> 00:24:13.260
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Racing Diva.

00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:15.800
The fun is only getting started!
